<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9439f29e7fab8d97163c950e9bb7714b84ee4231" commit="f87179261ebc45e4d172951df15f8880d454bd80" commit_message="Revert most recent TP config  The previous config + FW combo was meant to fix some noise issues, but it appears to cause strange performance issues.  Namely latency increases dramatically when you add a second finger to the pad.  As such, this CL reverts back to the old version while we figure out a new solution.  The old version of the config is susceptible to noise, but is otherwise better than this config.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:62157 TEST=emerged and deployed on a Caroline, the touchpad worked much better after allowing the updater to apply this config. CQ-DEPEND=CL:*318646  Change-Id: I9439f29e7fab8d97163c950e9bb7714b84ee4231 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/430204 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="430204" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/04/430204/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I09f1cc586c644805a1e0e46a9649381228de543c" commit="02147a67761bf405c50bfc37de805f93794d5abd" commit_message="lakitu: disable shill USE flag  BUG=b:32763905 TEST=build_packages passes  Change-Id: I09f1cc586c644805a1e0e46a9649381228de543c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/430279 Commit-Ready: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="430279" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/79/430279/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idebb78baf7630ab6f2f0b16ef7c8f8430c02b14f" commit="9a7998c1dc4ba35bf92ec11c247bf3cff37f8e4e" commit_message="lakitu: add board_specific_setup.sh identical to one in private overlay  BUG=b:32763905 TEST=build_package &amp;&amp; build_image in overlay-lakitu  Change-Id: Idebb78baf7630ab6f2f0b16ef7c8f8430c02b14f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/430379 Commit-Ready: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="430379" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/79/430379/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I6b8a4e222e386eda14ba1d8f75a1e098ae42b76f" commit="4d6114a2283a9d07f81c1af9bb4474e3cb765d53" commit_message="BACKPORT: mwifiex: don't wait for main_process in shutdown_drv  main_process is not expected to be running when shutdown_drv function is called. currently we wait for main_process completion in the function.  Actually the caller has already made sure main_process is completed by performing below actions. (1) disable interrupts in if_ops-&gt;disable_int. (2) set adapter-&gt;surprise_removed = true, main_process wont be queued. (3) mwifiex_terminate_workqueue(adapter), wait for workqueue to be completed.  This patch removes redundant wait code and takes care of related cleanup.  Signed-off-by: Xinming Hu &lt;huxm@marvell.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@codeaurora.org&gt; (cherry picked from  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/wireless-drivers-next.git master  